n  focally  is 0 5cm from the nearest posterior margin  0 6cm from the nearest medial margin   1 0cm from the lateral margin  The remaining resection margins are more than 1 0cm from the tumor  The breast parenchyma also shows another gray white  firm  nodular lesion located 0 5cm anterior to the tumor and 1 0cm from the nearest inked anterior margin  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The consistency of the nodule is not as hard as the tumor  The breast parenchyma also shows nodular fibrosis located 1 0cm  inferior to the tumor and measuring 1 5cm in greatest dimension and extending up to the anterior  posterior  inferior  lateral and medial margins  The remaining area of breast parenchyma consists of admixed fatty tissue and dense pink white fibrous stroma  Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior end margins in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior end margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor with inked margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular lesion  anterior to the tumor  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma with nodular fibrosis  away from the tumor and inferior to the tumor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior end margin  Received in formalin  and labeled  right axillary contents   is a fragment of tan yellow  fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm  which on dissection shows several tan pink to tan gray possible lymph nodes measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The largest three lymph nodes are each serially sectioned and submitted entirely  but separately in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 cassettes for each lymph node  The remaining smaller lymph nodes are submitted in toto in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1A   RIGHT S