Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 19 07 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast lumpectomy with axillary contents                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE NOTE  The tumor has some features of medullary carcinoma and is present in microscopic foci and a larger focus measuring 0 4cm  Tumor is focally present at the inked deep margin centrally  4 of 12 slides contain foci of carcinoma  lateral and central regions   2  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMATOSIS  3  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS  ACUTE AND CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  LYMPH NODES  AXILLARY   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 17 OF 17 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 29 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in two separately labeled parts  Labeled  right breast  stitch marks medial border   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm lumpectomy specimen  containing a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm skin ellipse with a stitch designating the medial aspect on one surface  A 4 5cm long  healing incision is present on the skin ellipse  The specimen is inked black  In addition the superior aspect is inked yellow and the inferior aspect is inked green  Sectioning serially reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm irregular cavity partially filled with blood clot  1 0cm beneath the skin ellipse  The cavity is surrounded by up to 1 5cm wide  firm  white gray  focally yellow  gelatinous tissue extending to inferior resection margins  centrally  Grossly no obvious distinct tumor is present  Representative sections from the firmer areas  including the inked margins are submitted serially from lateral medial aspect  SECTION CODE  A C  lateral region D I  central region  including representative skin J K  medial region  Labeled  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  containing multiple lymph nodes  ranging in greatest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 2 2cm  The lymph nodes are soft and have white tan to tan yellow cut surfaces  Representative half of each lymph node and representative fibroadipose tissue are submitted in L through P  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMBULATORY GEN SURGICAL   ACC 4 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART A  AXILLARY CONTENTS PART B  RIGHT BREAST , Unchecked.
