NING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block A   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast   is a 21 x 18 x 4 5cm mastectomy specimen with a 6 x 4cm skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 2 x 2 x 1cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity with surrounding fibrous tissue located  2cm from the deep margin  but 0 8cm from the anterior margin  This biopsy cavity is located approximately 5cm lateral and inferior to the center of the nipple  As well  3cm superior from the first biopsy cavity is a second biopsy cavity  1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  with surrounding fibrous tissue  This biopsy cavity is 0 8cm from the anterior margin and  2cm from the posterior margin  Between the two biopsy cavities  1cm from the superior and 1 2cm from the inferior  is a tan white  irregular shaped  gritty mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  located 0 8cm from the anterior margin  A second mass  1 x 1 x 0 9cm  that is tan white  gritty and irregular shaped is located approximately 6cm superior to the nipple in the same vertical plane  8cm from the largest biopsy cavity  This second mass is  2cm from the closest  posterior  margin  The remaining breast parenchyma contains scattered ill defined fibrous areas  all of which are  2cm from the posterior margin  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail attached to the mass  These lymph nodes range in size from REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Section Code  A C  Representative sections of largest biopsy cavity and adjacent anterior margin  D E  Small nodule between two biopsy cavities and small biopsy cavity along with adjacent anterior margin  F  Small biopsy cavity with adjacent anterior margin  G  Region between two biopsy cavities  H I  Representative sections of second nodule  away from biopsy cavities  J  Representative section of closest  posterior  margin to the second nodule  K L  Representative sections of fibrous areas away from biopsy cavities and nodules  located in the medial portion of the specimen  M O  Largest lymph node  trisected  submitted entirely  P Q  Second largest lymph node  bivalved  submitted entirely  R S  Large lymph nodes  bivalved  submitted entirely in separate cassettes  T U  More axillary lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  upper inner quadrant  superficial tissue  left breast   are two fragments of fibrofatty tissue measuring 5 x 3 x 1 and 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  These specimens are inked and serially sectioned to reveal no focal abnormalities  Representative sections of the two fragments of tissue are submitted as cassette V  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional left axillary tissue   are multiple fragments of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue measuring 7 x 3 x 3cm in aggregate  The tissue is dissected to reveal two lymph nodes  one measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  the other measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  A radial section of the largest node and the entire smaller node are submitted in cassettes W  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional superficial tissue  upper outer quadrant  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 2 5cm fibrofatty fragment of tissue  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal no focal abnormalities  just unremarkable breast tissue  A representative section is submitted as cassette X  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  upper quadrant superficial mass   are multiple fragments of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue measuring 6 x 4 x 1 5cm in aggregate  The tissue is entirely submitted as cassettes Y HH  Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  GRAY OR 34 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST SUPERFICIAL TISSUE  UPPER INNER QUADRANT  PART C  AXILLARY TISSUE ADDITIONAL LEFT  PART D  BREAST SUPERFICIAL TISSUE  UPPER OUTER QUADRANT  PART E  BREAST SUPERFICIAL TO MASS  UPPER QUADRANT  , Unchecked.
