  the invasive component is of a paucicellular mucinous type  colloid carcinoma   BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL TISSUE AT 2 O CLOCK   EXCISION  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 2  EXTENSIVELY PRESENT ON 6 OF 10 SLIDES  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM AND PRESENT AT THE NEW  STITCHED  MARGIN  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   EXCISION  MICROMETASTASIS OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA  ONE NODE   SINGLE TINY CLUSTER OF SEVERAL DOZEN CYTOKERATIN POSITIVE TUMOR CELLS ON 1 OF 18 IMMUNOSTAINED LEVELS   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    SEE NOTE  NOTE  Tumor cells are not present on any of the six frozen section slides  or on any of the six hematoxylin and eosin stained sections of this node  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm yellow pink  irregular fibrofatty tissue with one localization wire in place  a short stitch designating superior  and a long stitch designating lateral  There is a second localization wire within the container  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green and lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm pink red hemorrhagic area  consistent with previous biopsy site  The tissue surrounding this area varies from yellow and chalky to white and fibrous  The biopsy site comes to within 0 8cm of the lateral margin  1 0cm from the superior margin  1 7cm from the medial margin and  2 0cm from the remaining margins  Adjacent to the biopsy site is a tan firm glistening ill defined area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  which comes to within 0 1cm of the medial margin  0 4cm of the posterior margin  1 0cm to the superior margin  and  1 5cm to the remaining margins  In addition to these areas  there are a few tan firm ovoid nodules ranging from 0 2cm to 0 5cm  A few of these nodules appear to abut margins  Representative sections are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity and tan irregular area from superior to inferior   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular area to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule to anterior medial margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue adjacent to intact wire   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  are submitted sequentially from superior to inferior  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm soft  tan yellow irregular portion of adipose tissue  On sectioning  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm lymph node  which has soft tan cut surfaces  The lymph node is entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  1A  1B  1C  1D and 1E  The frozen section remnants are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast additional tissue at 2 o clock   stitch marks new margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focal dense gray white fibrous tissue  which abuts the new margin  No discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities are identified  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1  1A 1B  1C  1D  1E  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  Gross Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Tim Robinson  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagno