Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 09 CLINICAL DATA  Previous biopsy showed infiltrating ductal carcinoma of the breast  The patient opted for mastectomy and Tamoxifen                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FAT NECROSIS  FIBROSIS  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  AND PIGMENT LADEN HISTIOCYTES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The deep and superficial fat resection margins are free of carcinoma  There is no evidence of malignancy in eight of eight lymph nodes examined  The specimen was re examined and no additional lymph nodes were identified  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FOCAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  FIBROSIS  AND MICROCYST FORMATION  3  SKIN WITH SCAR  Diagnosis by  Deborah S  Fleischhacker  MD ScD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 22 44                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 765 gram  right modified radical mastectomy specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  with an axillary tail  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  An overlying skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 13 6cm  with a 2 6cm linear scar  7 5cm from the nipple in the upper outer quadrant  The nipple and skin are grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a 3 0cm biopsy cavity  6 0cm from the nearest resection margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is yellow to tan pink with bands of white  firm  fibrous tissue diffusely extending throughout the specimen  No other firm areas are palpated  The axillary tail is sectioned to reveal multiple tan pink lymph nodes  ranging in size from 0 2cm to 0 5cm  Sectioning reveals one 0 5cm lymph node to have a tan to white  smooth cut surface  The remainder have a tan cut surface  Section Code A B   deep resection margin with biopsy cavity C D   superficial fat resection margin with biopsy cavity E H   biopsy cavity  radial sections I J   breast  two representative sections K   skin with scar  two representative sections L M   nipple  trisected  submitted in entirety N O   axillary lymph nodes  one half submitted X Y   additional axillary soft tissue Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  Kathleen Hamilton  ANP PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
