Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 AUG 02 ACCESSIONED ON  21 AUG 02 at 15 18 CLINICAL DATA  History of DCIS on right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 AUG 02 at 09 56                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm re excision specimen oriented per surgery as follows  short stitch denotes anterior  long stitch denotes lateral  bow tie denotes cephalad  superior   The specimen is inked as follows  anterior black  posterior blue  superior orange  inferior green  lateral red  and medial yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned parallel to the superior and inferior axis to reveal a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 6 x 0 6cm  The biopsy cavity is 0 3cm away from the anterior  black  margin  0 4cm from the posterior  blue  margin  0 8cm from superior  orange  margin  0 9cm from the inferior  green  margin  0 6cm from the medial  yellow  margin and 1 9cm away from the lateral  red  margin  The tissue lining the biopsy cavity has scattered areas of granular  tan  fibrotic tissue  The remainder of the tissue is fatty with no masses or other lesions identified  SECTION CODE  A I  representative sections of biopsy cavity with margins  J L  representative sections of tissue away from the biopsy cavity  Resident  NORMA RODRIGUEZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin Hughes MD PART   BREAST RIGHT  RE EXC