Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 12 07 CLINICAL DATA  63 year old with breast cancer  On REMOVED_DATE the right breast showed lobular neoplasia  atypical lobular hyperplasia   and the left breast showed DCIS  grade 3  with comedonecrosis  at the margin  In February of  REMOVED_CASE_ID  the left re excision showed invasive ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  WITH FLORID DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  SCAR  CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR BIOPSY SITE  BREAST AND AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY LYMPH NODE DISSECTION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS AND FOCAL ATYPIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE OR IN SITU CARCINOMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 18 OF 18 LYMPH NODES  SKIN WITH SCAR  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 19                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm simple mastectomy with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 3cm tan pink skin ellipse containing an eccentric 3 1cm nipple areolar complex  One portion of the nipple appears to contain a 1 0cm retraction  Orientation of the specimen is not possible  However the posterior is inked red all remaining margins are inked black  The overlying skin ellipse contains a 2 5cm well healed scar 3 4cm from the nearest areolar border and it appears to extend to the one skin margin which is now designated as 12 o clock  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white stellate firm lesion subjacent to the epidermal scar and 0 5cm from the designated 12 o clock margin and 0 9cm from the posterior margin  The remaining parenchyma contains a moderate amount of tan white firm  dense fibrous tissue which appears to extend to multiple inked margins including the posterior  This is admixed with approximately 40  tan yellow lobular fat  Within the dense white fibrous tissue a few purple firm cysts averaging REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Stellate lesion to posterior  B D  Stellate lesion to skin and anterior 12 o clock margin  E  Representative section of cyst  F  Representative section of parenchyma at the 9 o clock margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast and axillary resection   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm simple mastectomy with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 8cm wrinkled tan skin ellipse containing an eccentric 4 0cm nipple areolar complex and a 4 5cm well healed linear scar 1 5cm from the nipple areolar complex and 0 9cm from the closest skin margin  No orientation is given for the specimen so the deep margin is inked red  All other margins are inked black and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm biopsy cavity which has a surrounding  indurated border ranging from 0 1cm up to 1 5cm and consisting of bright yellow areas suggestive of fat necrosis and tan white firm stellate extensions projecting towards multiple margins  This biopsy cavity is 0 8cm from the posterior margin  0 8cm from the anterior margin closest to the epidermal scar  This is designated as 12 o clock  The remaining parenchyma consists of approximately 80  tan yellow lobular fat admixed with approximately 10  tan white firm dense fibrous tissue  No other lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  G H  Biopsy cavity to posterior margin  I  Biopsy cavity to closest anterior 12 o clock margin  J  Biopsy cavity to skin  K L  Representative sections away from biopsy cavity  6 o clock   Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan yellow lobular aggregate containing multiple rubbery lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes  M O  Whole lymph nodes  P  Representative sections node  Gross Description by  KRISTEN SMITH Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST AND AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 20 CLINICAL DATA  64 year old female status post a left  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  breast cancer in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   who now presents with two suspicious areas on mammogram of the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  1   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  95    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3  AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    WITH PAGETOID SPREAD INTO DUCTS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 7cm in greatest dimension on histologic section  slide A  and extends to the inked resection margin  The carcinoma infiltrates insidiously throughout much of the specimen  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  2  MILD INTRADUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA WITH FOCAL APOCRINE METAPLASIA  BREAST  RIGHT  2   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  90    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE 2 3   AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  10   WITH PAGETOID SPREAD INTO DUCTS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 3cm in greatest dimension on histologic section  slide J   and extends to within 0 1cm of the inked resection margin  No difinite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  2  SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  3  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  4  MILD FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  BOTH NODULES   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate parts  Labeled  Right breast   1  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 2cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue  with needle localizing wire in place  and accompanying specimen x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan  firm mass with ill defined borders  that extends to the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in A through F  with the tumor mass in A through C  Labeled  Right breast  2  is a 3 x 2 x 2cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue  with needle localizing wire in place and accompanying specimen x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a pink tan  firm  speckled white mass  that extends to the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  2  and saved frozen  The remaining specimen is submitted entirely in G through J  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  1  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  RIGHT BREAST  2  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Craig Scott Seidman  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
