 The nipple is mobile and measures 1 0cm in greatest dimension  The skin surface lateral to the areola shows a linear healed scar measuring 3 5cm in length  The skin surface medial to the areola also shows a linear healed scar measuring 2 0cm in length  The anterior surface of the breast is inked blue and the posterior is inked black  The breast parenchyma of the upper outer quadrant shows an irregularly outlined  gray white  firm to hard mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The mass is located 0 3cm from the inked posterior margin and 1 0cm from the inked anterior margin  The breast parenchyma underlying the healed scars shows diffuse fibrosis  Laterally  a fibrous area measures REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  and medially another fibrous area measures REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm  The breast parenchyma of the inner lower quadrant also shows fibrosis measuring 3 0cm in greatest dimension  The remaining breast parenchyma is mostly fatty  Obvious lymph nodes are not identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire tumor with surrounding breast parenchyma  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma with fibrosis  lateral to the areola and corresponding to the overlying scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma medial to the areola  corresponding to the overlying scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast  lower inner quadrant  from the area of fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral aspect of the breast adjacent to the long stitch  without lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday February 18   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 45 25PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Focally  the tumor cells sow moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Thursday February 19   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 03 48PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  151  to chromosome 17 signals  133  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday February 25   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 26 20PM By his her si