om 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 13     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 180 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Positive 79 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in three separately labeled parts  Labeled  Left breast  short stitch on superior  long stitch on lateral  double stitch on subareola duct   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm piece of breast parenchyma  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm stellate hard  white mass which extends grossly to the area designated  subareola duct  and focally to within 0 2cm of the deep margin  medially  Anteriorly and superiorly the mass extends to within 0 2cm of the inked area of the lumpectomy specimen  The resection margin designated  subareola duct  is frozen as FX 1  now A  Additional tissue is saved frozen  BRDU sample is taken and hormone receptor tissue is taken and tissue is given for research  B F  representative sections of deep inked margin from medial to lateral  G J  representative sections of firm  gritty  white mass from medial to lateral  G  with the adjacent deep margin   K  unremarkable breast parenchyma  Labeled  Additional left axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue from which multiple soft  REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension lymph nodes are dissected  entirely in L  Labeled  Left modified radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen  The breast is 20 x 12 x 4cm  The skin ellipse is REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm with a 1 0cm diameter unremarkable nipple and a 3 5cm diameter unremarkable areola  2 0cm superior and lateral to the nipple is a 6 0cm recently sutured incision  Deep to this is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm defect in the specimen which corresponds to the previously lumpectomy specimen  The defect is complete in this area without a deep margin  the deep margin of the previous lumpectomy is described by the surgeon as to the fascia   The skin ellipse also contains three slightly raised brown to purple macules  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm in greatest dimension  The remainder of the breast specimen contains soft  white yellow unremarkable breast parenchyma  The axillary tail is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  from which multiple soft  tan to pink lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension are dissected  SECTION CODE  M T  axillary tail lymph nodes  O and S  one lymph node each bisected  U V  representative deep resection margins  inferior to previous biopsy site W  representative section  inferior to lumpectomy defect X  representative sections of skin  anterior to lumpectomy defect Y  representative sections of nipple X  representative section of breast  at least 2 0cm from the lumpectomy incision  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST SUBAREOLAR RESECTION MARGIN   POSITIVE FOR INFILTRATING AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  William H  Yong  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST SUBAREOLAR DUCT PART B  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY PART C  COMPLETION LEFT TISSUE MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 AUG 01 ACCESSIONED ON  06 AUG 01 at 14 03 CLINICAL DATA  Calcifications on left mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE 1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE 1 AND COMMENT  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  ASSOCIATED WITH BENIGN AND NEOPLASTIC COMPONENTS  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED ON C F  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS 1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  measured from section E  Grade  1 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 1cm from the posterior  orange inked  margin of the specimen along a broad front  section E   Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Focally positive at the posterior  orange inked  margin of the specimen  Stains for receptors  Requested  COMMENT  The in situ carcinoma is present in 4 of 7 sections  C F  and has moderate to marked nuclear atypia  It has a secretory and  clinging  pattern in some areas and in other areas is associated with cystically dilated glands with flattened epithelium and thyroid colloid like secretions  This latter component is reminiscent of the appearance of the cystic hypersecretory hyperplasia carcinoma spectrum of lesions  The microcalifications associated with the in situ and invasive carcinomatous components are larger and denser than those within the fibrocystic areas  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR HALF  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FOCAL MODERATE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF IN SITU OR INVASIVE TUMOR  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR 