r  respectively  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel nodes   are four lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 3cm in greatest diameter  The excess fat is trimmed  one node is bivalved and frozen as FX 1  now submitted as G  Two nodes are frozen entirely as FX 2  now as H  and one node is bisected and frozen as FX 3  now as I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast additional medial tissue   are three unoriented portions of tan white fibrofatty breast tissue  6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm in aggregate  which are unoriented  Sectioning through the tissues reveals predominately tan white variegated tissue which has a gritty surface upon cutting  essentially all of the three pieces of tissue are involved by this process  Representative sections of the largest piece are submitted in cassettes J K  the medium sized piece in cassette L and the smallest piece in cassette M  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast final shaved margin lateral half of cavity   are multiple fragments of yellow tan fibrofatty fibrofatty tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm in aggregate  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes N U  with the most fibrous portions in cassette N  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin medial half of cavity   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm portion of unoriented yellow tan fibrofatty tissue  which is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes V W  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary dissection   is a 11 x 6 x 2cm aggregate of yellow tan adipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes  which are submitted entirely as follows  X  One node  fragmented  Y  Five nodes  Z  Five nodes  AA  Four nodes  BB 