Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 MAY 99 ACCESSIONED ON  10 MAY 99 at 13 13 CLINICAL DATA  Biopsy identified ductal carcinoma of the breast  right modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MULTIFOCAL  DIFFUSELY PRESENT ADJACENT TO AND AWAY FROM THE BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Definite lymphovascular invasion is not seen  The multifocal nature of the invasive carcinoma precludes accurate assessment of tumor size  although  the invasive tumor probably spans an area greater than 5cm  The margins of resection appear free of tumor  2  ALL  20  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 99 at 10 52                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number  is a 30 x 18 x 6cm right mastectomy specimen  with an 18 x 16cm tear drop shaped portion of skin present on the anterior surface  A 4 5cm partially healed surgical scar is present on the lower outer quadrant of the skin  The nipple is inverted  A vague 10 x 9cm firm area is identified by palpation  Cut sections reveal a firm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm firm  tan white mass beneath the area of the scar which is 1 5cm from the closest  deep  margin  Just medial inferior to this area is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm cavity filled with soft red brown blood clot  The remainder of the specimen shows yellow adipose tissue admixed with approximately 20 to 30  firm white fibrous tissue with focal cystic areas  Representative sections are submitted  A E  Representative firm area F  Deep margin  G I  Representative white fibrous tissue  remote from tumor  J  Additional deep margin  K  Representative nipple  L  Representative hemorrhagic cavity  M N  One lymph node bisected  O V  Each  one lymph node bisected  W Y  Lymph nodes and fat  Resident  STACEY L  MIKESELL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
